codex
The fused final kernel is doing the final projection itself and rereads the triangle values once per output-channel block. For `dim=384`, that is now the largest cost. I’m adding an alternate final path: Triton computes only output LayerNorm and gating once, then cuBLAS handles the dense `to_out` projection.
